 "equipment_type": "Multi-boiler plant controller (boiler staging)",
 "applies_to": "tekmar Boiler Control 284, which stages and modulates up to four boilers for heating and DHW loads.",
 "summary": "The tekmar 284 boiler staging control has BACnet IP built in on an RJ45 port (it can be switched to Modbus over RS-485 instead). In BAS application mode the BMS sends the target temperature, a setpoint call and pump requests; in the other modes the BMS can monitor and adjust a few settings. Per-boiler objects repeat for boilers 1-4.",
 "bacnet_transport": [
  "BACnet IP"
 ],
 "firmware": "Application software J1220x (per the PICS)",
 "default_device_instance": 0,
 "access_inferred": false,
 "notes": [
  "The manual prints the per-boiler objects once with an (n) placeholder (e.g. \"Boil (n) TYPE\", \"B(n) PUMP\", \"ENABLE B(n)\") and lists the instance for each of boilers 1-4; names here are written with (n) replaced by the boiler number.",
  "AI 15 ERROR returns a numeric code; the manual lists 0 = no error and codes for EEPROM, sensor, flow/combustion-air proof and tN4 bus faults.",
  "BV 2-5 use inverted logic: 0 = enable, 1 = disable.",
  "AV 5 accepts -85 °F to mean no BAS outdoor sensor.",
  "Temperatures are in °F."
 ],
 "integration": {
  "summary": "Set the 284 BAS Type to BACnet IP and give it a device ID and IP settings in the BAS menu. For full control put the 284 in BAS application mode, then write AV 0 setpoint and BV 0 setpoint call, plus BV 1 / BO 0 pump requests. In the other application modes, turn BAS Monitor on to read values and adjust the room and outdoor design settings.",
  "minimum_points": [
   {
    "ref": "BV 0",
    "why": "Setpoint call from the BMS (1 = call for heat)",
    "name": "BAS SETP CALL"
   },
   {
    "ref": "BV 1",
    "why": "Primary pump request (1 = on)",
    "name": "BAS PRIM PMP REQ"
   },
   {
    "ref": "AV 0",
    "why": "Target supply temperature, 60-225 °F",
    "name": "SETPOINT"
   },
   {
    "ref": "BI 6",
    "why": "Heat call active",
    "name": "HEAT CALL"
   },
   {
    "ref": "AI 0",
    "why": "Target temperature in use, °F",
    "name": "Boil TARG"
   },
   {
    "ref": "AI 3",
    "why": "Boiler plant supply temperature, °F",
    "name": "Boil SUP"
   },
   {
    "ref": "AI 4",
    "why": "Boiler plant return temperature, °F",
    "name": "Boil RET"
   },
   {
    "ref": "AI 15",
    "why": "Error code; 0 = no error",
    "name": "ERROR"
   }
  ],
  "enable": "BMS control needs Application Mode = BAS on the 284; then AV 0 sets the target temperature and BV 0 makes the setpoint call, BV 1 requests the primary pump(s) and BO 0 the DHW pump. In RSET, SETP, DDHW or EMS mode the BMS gets monitoring and setting adjustment only, and BAS Monitor must be set ON (Advanced access).",
  "heartbeat": null,
  "remote_sensors": "AV 5 takes an outdoor air temperature from the BAS; write -85 °F to mean no BAS sensor.",
  "setup": [
   "BAS Type = BACn selects BACnet IP over the RJ45 port; MODB switches to Modbus over RS-485.",
   "Device ID is entered as four number groups (0-4, 0-99, 0-99, 0-99); default 0,0,0,0.",
   "DHCP is ON by default; with DHCP off the default IP is 192.168.0.200, gateway 192.168.0.1, subnet 255.255.255.0.",
   "UDP port default 0xBAC0 (47808); BBMD foreign registration is set with BBMD TIME, IP and port.",
   "The BAS menu items need Advanced access, which requires the lock/unlock switch beside the display set to unlock.",
   "DeviceCommunicationControl password is tekmar."
  ],
  "gotchas": [
   "ENABLE B1-B4 (BV 2-5) are 0 = enable, 1 = disable.",
   "The PICS lists no segmentation support.",
   "Ethernet cable runs are limited to 150 ft for CAT-5E or 300 ft for CAT-6."
  ]
 },
